---
import SectionHead from '../components/SectionHead.astro';

const dose = [['12', 'weeks'], ['15', 'min / day'], ['5×', 'per week']];
const results = [
  { label: 'Little-finger abduction, imagined', pct: 35, physical: false },
  { label: 'Elbow flexion, imagined', pct: 13.5, physical: false },
  { label: 'Little-finger abduction, physical', pct: 53, physical: true },
];
// Bars are scaled to the largest result.
const maxPct = Math.max(...results.map((r) => r.pct));
const literature = [
  'Strength improvements after imagined contractions have been reported in several independent studies',
  'Motor imagery has been shown to reduce strength loss during limb immobilisation',
  'Imagery training has been associated with increased motor-cortex activity',
  'Meta-analytic evidence finds motor imagery improves maximal voluntary strength compared with no training',
  'Across the literature, physical resistance training produces larger and more reliable gains',
];
---
<section id="research" class="section border-t border-slate-200" aria-labelledby="res-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <SectionHead eyebrow="The research" title="Scientists got people stronger using imagined contractions alone" id="res-h">
      In one peer-reviewed 12-week study, healthy participants practised maximal contractions entirely in their imagination, five days a week. Their measured strength went up
    </SectionHead>

    <div class="grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-[1.1fr_0.9fr] md:gap-14">
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-5 self-start rounded-2xl bg-midnight p-7 text-bone md:sticky md:top-24">
        <p class="eyebrow text-slate-400">Ranganathan et al., 2004&nbsp;· study dose</p>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-3 gap-4">
          {dose.map(([v, k]) => (
            <div class="flex flex-col gap-1">
              <span class="num text-[clamp(1.7rem,3.4vw,2.6rem)]">{v}</span>
              <span class="eyebrow text-[0.75rem] leading-[1.35] text-slate-400">{k}</span>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
        <hr class="border-slate-700" />
        <p class="eyebrow text-slate-400">Reported strength change</p>
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-3" role="list">
          {results.map((r) => (
            <div class="grid grid-cols-[1fr_4.5rem] items-center gap-3 text-[0.9rem] sm:grid-cols-[11rem_1fr_4.5rem]" role="listitem">
              <span class="col-span-2 text-slate-300 sm:col-span-1">{r.label}</span>
              <div class="h-2.5 overflow-hidden rounded-full bg-slate-700"><div class:list={['h-full rounded-full', r.physical ? 'bg-slate-300' : 'bg-signal']} style={`width:${(r.pct / maxPct) * 100}%`}></div></div>
              <span class="text-right font-mono text-[0.85rem] tabular-nums text-bone">+{r.pct}%</span>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
        <p class="text-[0.86rem] leading-[1.5] text-slate-400">The 35% result came from little-finger strength in one 12-week study. Elbow-flexion strength increased 13.5% in the same study. Results vary. Physical resistance training produced larger gains</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <div class="max-w-[36em] space-y-4">
          <p>Alongside the strength changes, the researchers reported measurements consistent with increased cortical drive to the trained muscles. Nothing about the muscle itself had been loaded. What changed was the signal</p>
          <p>The wider literature points the same way, with the same honest limits</p>
        </div>
        <ul class="mt-7 flex flex-col">
          {literature.map((t) => (
            <li class="grid grid-cols-[22px_1fr] items-start gap-3 border-t border-slate-200 py-3.5 text-[0.98rem] last:border-b">
              <span class="mt-[7px] h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-full bg-signal" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <span>{t}</span>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-4 font-mono text-[0.78rem] leading-[1.5] text-slate-500">Ranganathan VK, Siemionow V, Liu JZ, Sahgal V, Yue GH. From mental power to muscle power: gaining strength by using the mind. Neuropsychologia. 2004;42(7):944–956</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
